tyle="fill:currentColor">80</text><line x1="25.4" y1="220.9" x2="29.4" y2="220.9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="220.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">82</text><line x1="25.4" y1="189.7" x2="29.4" y2="189.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="189.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">84</text><line x1="25.4" y1="158.6" x2="29.4" y2="158.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="158.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">86</text><line x1="25.4" y1="127.4" x2="29.4" y2="127.4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="127.4" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">88</text><line x1="25.4" y1="96.3" x2="29.4" y2="96.3" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="96.3" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">90</text><line x1="25.4" y1="65.1" x2="29.4" y2="65.1" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="65.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">92</text><line x1="25.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">94</text><text x="205.7" y="284" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">neutron number N</text><text x="25.4" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">proton number Z</text><line x1="284" y1="92.3" x2="292" y2="100.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="284" y1="100.3" x2="292" y2="92.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="96" y1="216.9" x2="104" y2="224.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="96" y1="224.9" x2="104" y2="216.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="296" y="86.3" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Th-232</text><text x="108" y="210.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Pb-208</text></svg>', 'Chart of proton number against neutron number marking thorium-232 (142 neutrons, 90 protons) and lead-208 (126 neutrons, 82 protons), the start and end of the decay series.'),
('a8dc90c9-ed64-51ce-839d-0f7a97cd6f73', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 30, 30, 'Fluorine-18 (proton number 9) decays by β⁺ emission. How many neutrons does the daughter nucleus contain?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Daughter: A = 18, Z = 9 − 1 = 8, so N = 18 − 8 = 10. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: β⁺ lowers Z. C1: N = A − Z. A1: N = 10.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('6f1aae70-0f78-5926-8cf9-197f6eb247d9', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 31, 31, 'A nucleus in an excited state emits a γ-ray. What is the effect on the nucleus?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Its energy decreases but its nucleon number and proton number are unchanged', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'γ emission removes excess energy only. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: energy lost. C1: A and Z unchanged. A1: A (Its energy decreases but its nucleon number and proton number are unchanged).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('6fdf779e-c48b-59a9-8b96-4ce0462e651c', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 32, 32, 'Beryllium-7 (proton number 4) decays by capturing one of its own inner electrons. What is the proton number of the daughter nucleus?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'p + e⁻ → n + ν, so Z = 4 − 1 = 3, which is lithium-7. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: a proton becomes a neutron. C1: Z falls by 1. A1: Z = 3.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('8c944de4-2a6f-5ab9-9fd3-b2d047eacfcf', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 33, 33, 'Which type of decay increases the neutron-to-proton ratio of a nucleus?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'β⁺ decay', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'β⁺ turns a proton into a neutron: N rises by 1, Z falls by 1. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: p → n. C1: ratio N/Z rises. A1: D (β⁺ decay).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e59a4c0c-f78b-5e99-a5d0-25fb35498ea7', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 34, 34, 'Two helium-3 nuclei fuse to form helium-4 and some protons. How many protons are released?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Nucleons: 3 + 3 − 4 = 2; charge: 2 + 2 − 2 = 2, so both are protons: 1 + 1 = 2. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: nucleon balance. C1: charge balance. A1: protons = 2.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('48ac31de-7c10-56f1-ad39-bf1b84f29ab0', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 35, 35, 'Radium-226 (proton number 88) emits an α-particle. Calculate the charge on the daughter nucleus in units of 10⁻¹⁷ C. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.376', '10⁻¹⁷ C', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Z = 88 − 2 = 86. Q = 86 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 1.38 × 10⁻¹⁷ C. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: daughter Z. C1: Q = Ze. A1: Q = 1.38 × 10⁻¹⁷ C.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('cc709ff9-0eb2-5ee5-8097-9a377721f990', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 36, 36, 'In β⁻ decay, how does the quark content of the nucleon change?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A down quark changes into an up quark', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'udd (neutron) → uud (proton). Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: udd → uud. C1: d → u. A1: B (A down quark changes into an up quark).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('253a41ef-a55b-5242-92c7-053b5b9a3c83', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 37, 37, 'A nucleus decays by α emission and then by two β⁻ emissions, ending as uranium-234 (proton number 92). What was the nucleon number of the original nucleus?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '238', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'β⁻ decays leave A unchanged and α removes 4: A = 234 + 4 = 238. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: work backwards. C1: β⁻ leaves A. C1: α adds 4 going back. A1: A = 238.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('ef683903-6fd9-5181-a0a4-e60a8144eb94', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 38, 38, 'Which quantities are conserved in β⁻ decay?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Charge, nucleon number and lepton number', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'An electron and an antineutrino keep lepton number zero. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: charge and nucleon number. C1: lepton number with antineutrino. A1: C (Charge, nucleon number and lepton number).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('dca9ad2a-b5f5-5159-90ce-e645dd7ef19e', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 39, 39, 'Carbon-11 (proton number 6) is a β⁺ emitter used in PET scanning. How many neutrons are in its daughter nucleus?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Daughter: A = 11, Z = 6 − 1 = 5, N = 11 − 5 = 6. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Z − 1. C1: N = A − Z. A1: N = 6.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('3125b370-8070-5532-a949-1b8989b5bc87', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 40, 40, 'Uranium-238 (proton number 92) decays to stable lead-206 (proton number 82). (a) Calculate the number of α decays. (b) Calculate the change in proton number caused by the α decays alone. (c) Calculate the number of β⁻ decays.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) (238 − 206) ÷ 4 = 8. (b) 8 × 2 = 16, giving Z = 92 − 16 = 76. (c) β⁻ decays raise Z: 82 − 76 = 6. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: α count. C1: Z after α decays. M1: β⁻ raise Z by 1. C1: β⁻ count. A1: β⁻ decays = 6.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4cf31e62-t fg4cf31e62-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4cf31e62-t">Uranium-238 to lead-206</title><desc id="fg4cf31e62-d">Chart of proton number against neutron number marking uranium-238 (146 neutrons, 92 protons) and lead-206 (124 neutrons, 82 protons).</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="88.2" y1="34" x2="88.2" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="147" y1="34" x2="147" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205.7" y1="34" x2="205.7" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.5" y1="34" x2="264.5" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="323.2" y1="34" x2="323.2" y2="252" style=