ominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">neutron number N</text><text x="25.4" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">proton number Z</text><line x1="331" y1="61.1" x2="339" y2="69.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="331" y1="69.1" x2="339" y2="61.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="72.4" y1="216.9" x2="80.4" y2="224.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="72.4" y1="224.9" x2="80.4" y2="216.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="343" y="55.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">U-238</text><text x="84.4" y="210.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Pb-206</text></svg>', 'Chart of proton number against neutron number marking uranium-238 (146 neutrons, 92 protons) and lead-206 (124 neutrons, 82 protons).'),
('11cdfcda-f266-548e-847c-21b9a3382341', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 41, 41, 'Plutonium-239 (proton number 94) absorbs a neutron and splits into barium-144 (proton number 56), another nucleus X and three neutrons. (a) Find the proton number of X. (b) Find the nucleon number of X. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '93', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Z = 94 − 56 = 38 (strontium). (b) A = 239 + 1 − 144 − 3 = 93. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: charge balance. C1: include absorbed neutron. M1: nucleon balance. C1: value. A1: A = 93.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('0f7b0543-cd4b-5dac-8a27-8daabb2a2fe1', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 42, 42, 'Americium-241 (proton number 95), used in smoke detectors, emits α-particles. (a) Write the proton and nucleon numbers of the daughter. (b) Calculate the number of neutrons in the daughter. (c) State why the daughter is a different element.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '144', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) A = 241 − 4 = 237, Z = 95 − 2 = 93. (b) N = 237 − 93 = 144. (c) Its proton number has changed. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: daughter A. C1: daughter Z. M1: N = A − Z. C1: value. B1: element set by Z. A1: N = 144.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('3ba95364-1f62-51f3-8f5a-5b43095cb50e', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 43, 43, 'Aluminium-27 (proton number 13) is bombarded with α-particles and forms phosphorus-30 plus a neutron. The phosphorus then decays by β⁺ emission to silicon. (a) Check the first equation balances. (b) Find the proton number of silicon. (c) Find its nucleon number. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '30', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Nucleon numbers: 27 + 4 = 31 and 30 + 1 = 31; proton numbers: 13 + 2 = 15 and 15 + 0 = 15. (b) Z = 15 − 1 = 14. (c) A is unchanged by β⁺: A = 30 + 0 = 30. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: balance shown. C1: phosphorus Z = 15. C1: silicon Z = 14. C1: A unchanged. A1: A = 30.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('448c349a-76d4-53e8-aa02-1dab5e6254e4', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 44, 44, 'Neptunium-237 (proton number 93) decays by α, then β⁻, then α, then α. (a) Find the nucleon number of the final nucleus. (b) Find its proton number. (c) Find the number of neutrons in it. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '137', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) A = 237 − 3 × 4 = 225. (b) Z = 93 − 2 + 1 − 2 − 2 = 88. (c) N = 225 − 88 = 137. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: A after three α. C1: Z changes. C1: value of Z. M1: N = A − Z. C1: value. A1: N = 137.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('0498eed2-3b4f-5563-a019-3903cf270bcf', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 45, 45, 'In the Sun, four protons are turned into one helium-4 nucleus, two neutrinos and some positrons. (a) Use nucleon number to show that no other nucleons are produced. (b) Use charge conservation to find the number of positrons.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 4 × 1 = 4, so the helium-4 nucleus uses all the nucleons. (b) Charge: 4 × (+1) = +2 + n × (+1), so n = 4 − 2 = 2. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: nucleon balance. M1: charge balance. C1: neutrinos carry no charge. C1: value. A1: positrons = 2.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('302ecdfe-0807-5999-9df6-c4a845276057', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 46, 46, 'A nucleus X decays by β⁻, then α, then α, ending as radium-226 (proton number 88). (a) Work backwards to find the nucleus before the last α decay. (b) Find the nucleon number of X. (c) Find the proton number of X. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '91', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) A = 226 + 4 = 230, Z = 88 + 2 = 90. (b) A = 230 + 4 = 234 (unchanged by β⁻). (c) Before the first α: Z = 92; β⁻ raised Z by 1, so X had Z = 88 + 2 + 2 − 1 = 91. Mark scheme (6 marks). M1: reverse each step. C1: before last α. C1: nucleon number. C1: undo β⁻. C1: value. A1: Z = 91.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('475eca71-b30f-52a9-a03b-f475ebc81fdd', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 47, 47, 'Strontium-90 (proton number 38) decays by β⁻ to yttrium, which decays by β⁻ again. (a) Find the number of neutrons in strontium-90. (b) Find the proton number of the final product. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '40', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) N = 90 − 38 = 52. (b) Each β⁻ adds 1 to Z: Z = 38 + 1 + 1 = 40, which is zirconium-90. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: N = A − Z. M1: β⁻ raises Z. C1: value. B1: A stays 90. A1: Z = 40.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('186c6000-ca4a-5c7c-9476-76cb145a0951', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 48, 48, 'Uranium-235 (proton number 92) decays to lead-207 (proton number 82) by α and β⁻ decays. (a) Find the number of α decays. (b) Find the number of β⁻ decays.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) (235 − 207) ÷ 4 = 7. (b) After 7 α decays Z = 92 − 14 = 78, so β⁻ decays = 82 − 78 = 4. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: α count. C1: Z after α. M1: β⁻ raise Z. C1: value. A1: β⁻ decays = 4.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgb7d5da23-t fgb7d5da23-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgb7d5da23-t">Uranium-235 to lead-207</title><desc id="fgb7d5da23-d">Chart of proton number against neutron number marking uranium-235 (143 neutrons, 92 protons) and lead-207 (125 neutrons, 82 protons).</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="88.2" y1="34" x2="88.2" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="147" y1="34" x2="147" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205.7" y1="34" x2="205.7" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.5" y1="34" x2="264.5" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="323.2" y1="34" x2="323.2" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="252" x2="382" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="220.9" x2="382" y2="220.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="189.7" x2="382" y2="189.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="158.6" x2="382" y2="158.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="127.4" x2="382" y2="127.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="96.3" x2="382" y2="96.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="65.1" x2="382" y2="65.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="382" y2="34" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="252" x2="388" y2="252" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="252" x2="29.4" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,252 385.7,255 385.7,249" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="29.4,24 32.4,30.3 26.5,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="29.4" y1="252" x2="29.4" y2="256" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="29.4" y="264" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">120</text><line x1="88.2" y1="252" x2="88.2" y2="256" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="88.2" y="264" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">125</text><line x1="147" y1="252" x2="147" y2="256" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="147" y="264" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">130</text><line x1="205.7" y1="252" x2="205.7" y2="256" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="205.7" y="264" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">135</text><line x1="264.5" y1="252" x2="264.5" y2="256" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="264.5" y="264" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">140</text><line x1="323.2" y1="252" x2="323.2" y2="256" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="323.2" y="264" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">145</text><line x1="382" y1="252" x2="382" y2="256" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="382" y="264" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">150</text><line x1="25.4" y1="252" x2="29.4" y2="252" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="252" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">80</text><line x1="25.4" y1="220.9" x2="29.4" y2="220.9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="220.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">82</text><line x1="25.4" y1="189.7" x2="29.4" y2="189.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="189.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">84</text><line x1="25.4" y1="158.6" x2="29.4" y2="158.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="158.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">86</text><line x1="25.4" y1="127.4" x2="29.4" y2="127.4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="127.4" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">88</text><line x1="25.4" y1="96.3" x2="29.4" y2="96.3" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="96.3" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">90</text><line x1="25.4" y1="65.1" x2="29.4" y2="65.1" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="65.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">92</text><line x1="25.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">94</text><text x="205.7" y="284" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">neutron number N</text><text x="25.4" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">proton number Z</text><line x1="295.7" y1="61.1" x2="303.7" y2="69.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="295.7" y1="69.1" x2="303.7" y2="61.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84.2" y1="216.9" x2="92.2" y2="224.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="84.2" y1="224.9" x2="92.2" y2="216.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="307.7" y="55.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">U-235</text><text x="96.2" y="210.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Pb-207</text></svg>', 'Chart of proton number against neutron number marking uranium-235 (143 neutrons, 92 protons) and lead-207 (125 neutrons, 82 protons).'),
('62adfe92-873a-5842-985a-f0197d730179', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 49, 49, 'In a reactor, uranium-238 (proton number 92) absorbs a neutron and then undergoes two β⁻ decays. (a) Find the nucleon number of the nucleus formed after neutron capture. (b) Find the proton number of the final nucleus. (c) Name the element formed, given that Z = 94 is plutonium. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '94', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) A = 238 + 1 = 239. (b) Z = 92 + 1 + 1 = 94. (c) Plutonium-239. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: neutron capture adds 1 to A. C1: Z unchanged by capture. M1: each β⁻ adds 1. C1: value. B1: plutonium. A1: Z = 94.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('1c3df52f-b61a-5b57-b459-393db07f98a1', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '20eb2251-a133-4766-96d3-065fb00dfd07', 'a-level', '29.1', '9702 coursebook 29.1 · Balanced equations', 50, 50, 'Polonium-210 (proton number 84) emits an α-particle. (a) Find the proton number of the daughter. (b) Calculate the charge on the daughter nucleus. (c) Show that charge is conserved. Give only the answer to (b), in units of 10⁻¹⁷ C. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.312', '10⁻¹⁷ C', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Z = 84 − 2 = 82. (b) Q = 82 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 1.31 × 10⁻¹⁷ C. (c) 82e + 2e = 84e. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: Z. M1: Q = Ze. C1: value. B1: charge balance. A1: Q = 1.31 × 10⁻¹⁷ C.', 5, NULL, NULL)
