('7ef749d1-3b58-5e88-847c-42c7751f00ee', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 32, 32, 'From the binding energy per nucleon curve, which process can release energy?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Fusion of light nuclei and fission of heavy nuclei', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Both move nuclei towards the peak near A = 56. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: light nuclei fuse. C1: heavy nuclei split. A1: C (Fusion of light nuclei and fission of heavy nuclei).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1af37a99-t fg1af37a99-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1af37a99-t">Binding energy per nucleon</title><desc id="fg1af37a99-d">Graph of binding energy per nucleon against nucleon number: it rises steeply for light nuclei, peaks at about 8.8 MeV near A = 56 and falls slowly to about 7.6 MeV for the heaviest nuclei.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="104" y1="34" x2="104" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="178.5" y1="34" x2="178.5" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="253" y1="34" x2="253" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="327.5" y1="34" x2="327.5" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="402" y1="34" x2="402" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke