81.5 348.4,81.8 351.3,82.1 354.3,82.5 357.3,82.8 360.3,83.2 363.3,83.5 366.2,83.8 369.2,84.2 372.2,84.5 375.2,84.8 378.2,85.2 381.1,85.5 384.1,85.8 387.1,86.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Graph of binding energy per nucleon against nucleon number: it rises steeply for light nuclei, peaks at about 8.8 MeV near A = 56 and falls slowly to about 7.6 MeV for the heaviest nuclei.'),
('41063056-1618-560d-9af9-2de4ff206b5a', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 33, 33, 'A nucleus has a binding energy of 1784 MeV. Taking 1 u as 931.5 MeV, calculate its mass defect in u.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.915', 'u', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Δm = 1784 ÷ 931.5 = 1.92 u. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Δm = BE ÷ 931.5. C1: value. A1: Δm = 1.92 u.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('b39a0c33-98d5-5187-800a-17d6ac5f7082', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 34, 34, 'Which reaction releases energy?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Two light nuclei combining into a nucleus with a higher binding energy per nucleon', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Energy is released when the products are more tightly bound. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: increase in BE per nucleon. C1: releases energy. A1: A (Two light nuclei combining into a nucleus with a higher binding energy per nucleon).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('ae03b28c-0572-54d1-bfce-8c5d7e5c4ddb', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 35, 35, 'Helium-4 has a binding energy of 28.30 MeV and helium-3 a binding energy of 7.72 MeV. How much energy is needed to remove one neutron from helium-4?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '20.58', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = 28.30 − 7.72 = 20.58 MeV. Mark scheme (3 marks). M1: difference in binding energies. C1: value. A1: E = 20.58 MeV.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('0304df6b-2561-503b-a90a-c4a5fe49d0b1', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 36, 36, 'Iron-56 contains 26 protons and 30 neutrons, and its nucleus has a mass of 55.920674 u. With mₚ = 1.007276 u, mₙ = 1.008665 u and 1 u equivalent to 931.5 MeV, find the binding energy per nucleon.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '8.79', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Δm = 26 × 1.007276 + 30 × 1.008665 − 55.920674 = 0.52845 u. BE = 0.52845 × 931.5 = 492.25 MeV. BE/A = 492.25 ÷ 56 = 8.79 MeV. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: mass defect. C1: BE. C1: ÷ 56. A1: BE/A = 8.79 MeV.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('97e7cb46-0625-516f-8b75-51991b8ed816', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 37, 37, 'Why does the binding energy per nucleon decrease for very heavy nuclei?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The electrostatic repulsion between the many protons grows, while the strong force acts only between near neighbours', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Coulomb repulsion acts across the whole nucleus. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: proton repulsion long range. C1: strong force short range. A1: D (The electrostatic repulsion between the many protons grows, while the strong force acts only between near neighbours).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('259d6831-2a2f-587e-862f-a26d6c941923', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 38, 38, 'A nucleus has a mass defect of 5.0 × 10⁻²⁹ kg. Calculate its binding energy in units of 10⁻¹² J. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.5', '10⁻¹² J', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'BE = Δm c² = 5.0 × 10⁻²⁹ × (3.00 × 10⁸)² = 4.5 × 10⁻¹² J. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: E = mc². C1: value. A1: BE = 4.5 × 10⁻¹² J.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('c2e44718-c8f2-5de6-aeaf-1c237d2b5dea', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 39, 39, 'How strongly, on average, is each nucleon held in uranium-238, whose total binding energy is 1802 MeV? Give the binding energy per nucleon in MeV.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7.571', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'BE/A = 1802 ÷ 238 = 7.57 MeV. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: ÷ 238. C1: value. A1: BE/A = 7.57 MeV.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('ceda4a2d-3d11-5759-9bb3-1a4fadb4614c', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 40, 40, 'Which statement about the mass defect is correct?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It is the difference between the mass of the separate nucleons and the mass of the nucleus', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Δm = Zmₚ + Nmₙ − M(nucleus). Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: definition. C1: positive for bound nuclei. A1: B (It is the difference between the mass of the separate nucleons and the mass of the nucleus).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('66b67dd7-b770-5bf6-993f-eb2391573a21', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 41, 41, 'Deuterium (binding energy 2.22 MeV) and tritium (binding energy 8.48 MeV) fuse into helium-4 (binding energy 28.30 MeV) and a neutron. Calculate the energy released.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '17.6', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = 28.30 − (2.22 + 8.48) = 17.6 MeV. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: BE after − BE before. C1: neutron has no binding energy. C1: value. A1: E = 17.6 MeV.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('7a1c5f83-657f-51e8-91bc-c437b9f68fc0', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 42, 42, 'Helium-3 is made of two protons and one neutron; its nucleus has a mass of 3.014932 u. With mₚ = 1.007276 u, mₙ = 1.008665 u and 1 u equivalent to 931.5 MeV, how much energy binds it together?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7.717', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Δm = 2 × 1.007276 + 1.008665 − 3.014932 = 0.008285 u. BE = 0.008285 × 931.5 = 7.72 MeV. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: mass defect. C1: × 931.5. A1: BE = 7.72 MeV.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('0c7ce40f-d3fa-51c3-9bdf-a1697af5f92d', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 43, 43, 'An oxygen-16 nucleus (8 protons, 8 neutrons) has a mass of 15.990526 u. Taking a proton as 1.007276 u, a neutron as 1.008665 u and 1 u as 931.5 MeV: (a) calculate the mass defect; (b) calculate the binding energy; (c) calculate the binding energy per nucleon. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7.976', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Δm = 8 × 1.007276 + 8 × 1.008665 − 15.990526 = 0.13700 u. (b) BE = 0.13700 × 931.5 = 127.6 MeV. (c) 127.6 ÷ 16 = 7.98 MeV. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: nucleon masses. C1: mass defect. C1: BE. C1: ÷ 16. A1: BE/A = 7.98 MeV.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('dd822b75-d9f5-5e82-850e-f4d3b55daa6d', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 44, 44, 'In one fission, uranium-236 (binding energy 7.59 MeV per nucleon) splits into xenon-140 (8.29 MeV per nucleon), strontium-94 (8.59 MeV per nucleon) and two neutrons. (a) Calculate the total binding energy of uranium-236. (b) Calculate the total binding energy of the fragments. (c) Calculate the energy released. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '176.8', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 236 × 7.59 = 1791.2 MeV. (b) 140 × 8.29 + 94 × 8.59 = 1968.1 MeV. (c) 1968.1 − 1791.2 = 177 MeV. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: BE of U. C1: BE of Xe. C1: BE of Sr. M1: difference. C1: value. A1: E = 177 MeV.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1013e6f8-t fg1013e6f8-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1013e6f8-t">Fission fragments</title><desc id="fg1013e6f8-d">Binding energy per nucleon curve with uranium-236 (7.59 MeV), xenon-140 (8.29 MeV) and strontium-94 (8.59 MeV) marked.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="104" y1="34" x2="104" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="178.5" y1="34" x2="178.5" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="253" y1="34" x2="253" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="327.5" y1="34" x2="327.5" y2="252" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;f