 348.4,81.8 351.3,82.1 354.3,82.5 357.3,82.8 360.3,83.2 363.3,83.5 366.2,83.8 369.2,84.2 372.2,84.5 375.2,84.8 378.2,85.2 381.1,85.5 384.1,85.8 387.1,86.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="108.9" y1="55.4" x2="116.9" y2="63.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="108.9" y1="63.4" x2="116.9" y2="55.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="380.1" y1="81.8" x2="388.1" y2="89.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="380.1" y1="89.8" x2="388.1" y2="81.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="118.9" y="75.4" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Fe-56</text><text x="378.1" y="101.8" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">U-238</text></svg>', 'Binding energy per nucleon curve with iron-56 near the peak and uranium-238 at the heavy end marked.'),
('3dad9c2e-c1cc-5923-9b66-9ba59fe37346', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 48, 48, 'Nickel-58 (28 protons, 30 neutrons) has a binding energy per nucleon of 8.73 MeV. Taking a proton as 1.007276 u, a neutron as 1.008665 u and 1 u as 931.5 MeV: (a) calculate its total binding energy; (b) calculate its mass defect in u; (c) calculate the mass of the nucleus in u. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '57.92', 'u', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) BE = 58 × 8.73 = 506.34 MeV. (b) Δm = 506.34 ÷ 931.5 = 0.54357 u. (c) M = 28 × 1.007276 + 30 × 1.008665 − 0.54357 = 57.92010 u. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: total BE. C1: mass defect. C1: mass of nucleons. M1: subtract. C1: value. A1: M = 57.92010 u.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('c775cc10-56be-5f99-9ac3-88f31ee06ed5', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 49, 49, 'Each fission of uranium-235 releases 177 MeV. (a) Calculate the number of nuclei in 1.0 kg of uranium-235 (molar mass 0.235 kg mol⁻¹). (b) Calculate the energy released if all of them undergo fission, in units of 10¹³ J. Take N_A = 6.02 × 10²³ mol⁻¹. Take 1 MeV = 1.60 × 10⁻¹³ J.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7.255', '10¹³ J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) N = 1.0 ÷ 0.235 × 6.02 × 10²³ = 2.562 × 10²⁴. (b) E = 2.562 × 10²⁴ × 177 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹³ = 7.25 × 10¹³ J. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: moles. C1: nuclei. M1: × energy per fission in J. C1: value. A1: E = 7.25 × 10¹³ J.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('4df25d10-865c-5fa7-a214-392f5844425c', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', 'c7d1948a-561e-56c0-8776-090012819a77', 'a-level', '29.4', '9702 coursebook 29.4 · Mass defect and binding energy', 50, 50, 'Polonium-210 (binding energy 1645.2 MeV) decays into lead-206 (1622.3 MeV) and helium-4 (28.3 MeV). (a) Calculate the total binding energy of the products. (b) Calculate the energy released in the decay. (c) Explain why the decay can occur. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5.4', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 1622.3 + 28.3 = 1650.6 MeV. (b) E = 1650.6 − 1645.2 = 5.4 MeV. (c) The products are more tightly bound in total, so energy is released. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: products. M1: difference. C1: value. B1: products more tightly bound. B1: energy released spontaneously. A1: E = 5.4 MeV.', 6, NULL, NULL)
